; End of the game: dead, or the ending text printed
;
; Entered when the player dies (#R$977F KillCharacter) and from several handlers
; that kill the player. Sets the actor to the player and prints "You are dead.",
; then the score (#R$83F5; the mark of how much of the adventure was done), waits
; for a key and restarts the game at #R$6C27. The victory (#R$A9D6) joins at
; EndGame_Wait after its own text.
; .
; Hardware: reads the keyboard port $FE (all half-rows) in a polling loop.
@label=EndGame
c$90D2 SUB A                ; A = 0
 $90D3 LD ($B6EA),A         ; actor = the player
 $90D6 LD HL,$AFF1          ; "<subject> is dead."
 $90D9 CALL $72DD
 $90DC CALL $83F5           ; "You have mastered ..% Of this adventure."
; Entry point of #R$A9D6 (the victory): wait for any key.
@label=EndGame_Wait
*$90DF XOR A                ; A = 0 selects every half-row
@isub=IN A,(PORT_ULA)
 $90E0 IN A,($FE)
@isub=AND KEY_BITS
 $90E2 AND $1F
@isub=CP KEY_BITS
 $90E4 CP $1F
 $90E6 JR Z,$90DF
 $90E8 JP $6C27             ; restart the game
